# Fblthp's ability is on the stack already when Shock kills him (CR 603.2), so it still resolves and Bot1 draws two cards.
# The card in the graveyard is a new object, so it does not move (CR 400.7), but its owner's library is still shuffled
# because the ability refers to that specific object (CR 701.24c). Fblthp stays in the graveyard. The Shock is
# cast in the combat damage step, after the damage that triggered the ability has been dealt.

[Bot1 Deck]
Fblthp, Impossibly Lost
Island x19

[Bot2 Deck]
Shock
Mountain x3
Island x16

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Island.Play
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Island.Play
Bot1.Hand.Fblthp, Impossibly Lost.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Island#1.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Island#2.Activate
[T4 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Mountain.Play
[T5 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Attack(Fblthp, Impossibly Lost > Bot2)
[T5 Bot1.CombatDamage]
Bot2.Hand.Shock.Cast(Fblthp, Impossibly Lost)
Bot2.Battlefield.Mountain.Activate
[T5 Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot2.Life = 19
Bot1.Graveyard = Fblthp, Impossibly Lost
Bot1.Battlefield.Count = 2
Bot1.Library.Count = 9
Result = InProgress
